WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.738
It was fall at Green Gables. Anne and Diana Barry were resting in a sunny corner of the Green Gables orchard. They had been picking apples.

2
00:00:11.739 --> 00:00:17.413
"It's been a nice summer," said Diana, "and Miss Lavender's wedding was the highlight.

3
00:00:17.414 --> 00:00:21.059
Winter will be awfully dull with you and Gilbert gone."

4
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.424
"Fred will be here," said Anne teasingly.

5
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:33.352
"Still, I can't believe you leave next week!" said Diana for the hundredth time. "I'll be so lonely."

6
00:00:33.353 --> 00:00:40.118
"It's me who'll be lonely!" said Anne. "I don't know anyone at Redmond College."

7
00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:47.435
"Except Gilbert—and Charlie Sloane," said Diana, teasing Anne the way Anne had teased her.

8
00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:53.770
"Charlie Sloane will be a great comfort," Anne said sarcastically, and they both laughed.

9
00:00:53.771 --> 00:00:57.585
Diana knew that Anne did not enjoy Charlie's attention.

10
00:00:57.586 --> 00:01:01.191
Both girls were less sure of how Anne felt about Gilbert.

11
00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:08.186
They were great friends, but Gilbert had been expressing some romantic interest in Anne lately.

12
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:13.307
Diana soon returned home, and Anne went to the post office.

13
00:01:13.308 --> 00:01:19.526
There she picked up a letter she'd received from Priscilla Grant, a friend that Anne had made at Queen's College.

14
00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:24.071
As Anne walked home, reading the letter, she bumped into Gilbert Blythe.

15
00:01:24.072 --> 00:01:27.846
"Gilbert!" Anne said excitedly, holding out the letter.

16
00:01:27.847 --> 00:01:32.322
"Priscilla Grant is going to Redmond College too!"

17
00:01:32.323 --> 00:01:36.396
"I think we'll be very happy at the college, Anne," said Gilbert.

18
00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:41.674
"I've heard Halifax is a nice old town with many beautiful parks and magnificent scenery."

19
00:01:41.675 --> 00:01:50.895
"I wonder if it will be—can be—any more beautiful than this," murmured Anne, looking around her.

20
00:01:50.896 --> 00:01:54.463
Gilbert and Anne leaned on the bridge near the old pond.

21
00:01:54.464 --> 00:01:57.955
"You are very quiet, Anne," said Gilbert at last.

22
00:01:57.956 --> 00:02:01.176
He covered Anne's slender hand with his own.

23
00:02:01.177 --> 00:02:06.797
His hazel eyes grew dark, and he opened his mouth to speak of his love for Anne.

24
00:02:06.798 --> 00:02:14.822
But Anne snatched her hand away and turned quickly. "I must go home!" she exclaimed.

25
00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:18.882
She chattered away until they parted a few minutes later.

26
00:02:18.883 --> 00:02:25.950
"I never felt glad to see Gilbert go before," she thought as she walked alone up the lane to Green Gables.

27
00:02:25.951 --> 00:02:34.631
"Our friendship will be spoiled if he goes on with this nonsense. Why can't boys just be sensible?"

28
00:02:34.632 --> 00:02:42.522
The following week went quickly. The Avonlea Improvement Society gave a farewell party in honor of Anne and Gilbert.

29
00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:47.144
Everyone was there: Diana Barry, rosy and dimpled, together with Fred;

30
00:02:47.145 --> 00:02:53.142
Jane Andrews, neat and sensible; Ruby Gillis, pretty with red geraniums in her golden hair;

31
00:02:53.143 --> 00:02:59.735
and Gilbert Blythe and Charlie Sloane, both trying to stay as close to Anne as possible.

32
00:02:59.736 --> 00:03:04.685
Anne enjoyed the evening tremendously, but at the end it was spoiled.

33
00:03:04.686 --> 00:03:09.506
On the veranda Gilbert tried again to say something romantic to her.

34
00:03:09.507 --> 00:03:15.358
Anne was so annoyed that later, to punish him, she decided to walk home with Charlie Sloane.

35
00:03:15.359 --> 00:03:22.074
When she looked to see if her punishment was working, Anne saw Gilbert leaving with the beautiful Ruby Gillis.

36
00:03:22.075 --> 00:03:27.968
She felt a small knot in her stomach—her punishment had backfired!

37
00:03:27.969 --> 00:03:34.986
A week later it was Monday, the day that Anne, Gilbert, and Charlie were to leave for Redmond College.

38
00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:42.248
Rain poured down, and Mrs. Lynde, Marilla, Dora, and Anne were quietly eating breakfast.

39
00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:49.325
For the first time ever, Davy did not eat, but instead spent the meal crying into his porridge.

40
00:03:49.326 --> 00:03:53.649
Afterwards Marilla and Mrs. Lynde kissed Anne good-bye.

41
00:03:53.650 --> 00:04:00.304
Dora squeezed out two tears and kissed Anne primly, but Davy refused to say good-bye at all.

42
00:04:00.305 --> 00:04:04.259
Instead he ran and hid in the cupboard.

43
00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.939
Diana arrived with the horse and buggy, and Anne climbed in.

44
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:13.562
Davy's muffled cries were the last sounds Anne heard as she left Green Gables.

45
00:04:13.563 --> 00:04:19.634
When they arrived at the Avonlea train station, Charlie and Gilbert were waiting on the platform.

46
00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:28.478
Anne just had time to check her luggage, show her ticket, and say a hurried good-bye to Diana before the train left for Charlottetown.

47
00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:35.132
Anne, Charlie, and Gilbert got off the train at Charlottetown and boarded the ferry bound for Nova Scotia.

48
00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:41.454
As the ferry left the harbor, the sun came out, and Anne felt a little less homesick.

49
00:04:41.455 --> 00:04:47.014
Charlie became so seasick that Anne and Gilbert were left alone on the deck.

50
00:04:47.015 --> 00:04:56.156
"Oh, Gilbert," said Anne. "I do hope I'll like Redmond College, but I'm sure I won't!"

51
00:04:56.157 --> 00:05:00.318
"Anne, that's not like you!" Gilbert said, surprised.

52
00:05:00.319 --> 00:05:04.329
"I've always longed to go to college," said Anne.

53
00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:08.694
"But now that I am, I wish I wasn't!" She paused.

54
00:05:08.695 --> 00:05:12.654
"I'll have a good cry and then I should feel better."

55
00:05:12.655 --> 00:05:17.559
Anne walked to other end of the deck and did just that.

56
00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:23.393
It was nine o'clock that night when the boat reached Halifax, and they found themselves in the crowded port.

57
00:05:23.394 --> 00:05:31.107
Anne felt horribly bewildered, but before long Priscilla Grant, who had come to Halifax on Saturday, grabbed her.

58
00:05:31.108 --> 00:05:39.826
"Here you are, Anne!" said Priscilla with a smile. "And I suppose you're pretty tired."

59
00:05:39.827 --> 00:05:47.924
"Tired!" Anne exclaimed. "Priscilla, if you weren't here, I think I would just sit down on my suitcase and cry!"

60
00:05:47.925 --> 00:05:53.741
Priscilla smiled and said, "Is that Gilbert Blythe over there, Anne? He's grown up!

61
00:05:53.742 --> 00:05:57.966
And of course that's Charlie Sloane. He hasn't changed."

62
00:05:57.967 --> 00:06:04.404
Anne and Priscilla waved good-bye to Gilbert and Charlie and got in a cab.

63
00:06:04.405 --> 00:06:08.117
"We're staying in a lovely boardinghouse, Anne," Priscilla said,

64
00:06:08.118 --> 00:06:14.362
"Our landladies are lovely too—Miss Hannah Harvey and Miss Ada Harvey. They're twins."

65
00:06:14.363 --> 00:06:20.804
"I can't get away from twins," Anne said, smiling as she thought of Davy and Dora.

66
00:06:20.805 --> 00:06:33.925
Then she and Priscilla set off toward their new home and new life in Halifax.

